# Gorbe

Interactive command-line scaffolder for Python web projects. Answer a few
prompts and Gorbe creates the project, installs dependencies, writes the
application files, optionally adds Docker support, and initializes Git.

```
$ gorbe
? Project name: my-app
? Framework: FastAPI
? Database: PostgreSQL
? Package manager: uv (recommended)
? Generate Docker files? yes
? Database name: app
? Database user: app
? Database password: app
? MySQL root password: root
```

The same thing can be run non-interactively:

```bash
gorbe \
  --name my-app \
  --framework fastapi \
  --database postgresql \
  --manager uv \
  --docker \
  --db-name app \
  --db-user app \
  --db-password secret
```

## Features

- **FastAPI** — `app/` package with an application entrypoint, router, models,
  schemas, and async SQLAlchemy database setup.
- **Flask** — `app/` package with an application entrypoint and Flask-SQLAlchemy
  setup.
- **Django** — scaffolded with `django-admin startproject`.
- **Package managers** — `uv` or `pip` with a virtual environment.
- **Databases** — SQLite, MySQL, and PostgreSQL.
- **Docker (optional)** — `Dockerfile`, `.dockerignore`, and
  `docker-compose.yaml`, including a database service, healthcheck, and volume.
- **Project hygiene** — `.gitignore`, `requirements.txt`, and a Git repository.
- **Installer** — package as a single binary with PyInstaller.

## Requirements

- Python 3.12 or newer
- Git
- `uv` when using the uv workflow
- Docker when generating and running Docker files

## Installation

### From source

With uv:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/sudo-cat-coder/gorbe.git
cd gorbe
uv sync
uv run gorbe
```

With pip:

```bash
git clone https://github.com/sudo-cat-coder/gorbe.git
cd gorbe
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .
gorbe
```

### Build a standalone binary

Linux / macOS:

```bash
uv sync --extra build
uv run pyinstaller --clean --noconfirm gorbe.spec
chmod +x install.sh
./install.sh
```

Windows:

```powershell
uv sync --extra build
uv run pyinstaller --clean --noconfirm gorbe.spec
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\install.ps1
```

The installers expect the built binary in `dist/`. On Linux/macOS it is copied
to `/usr/local/bin`; on Windows it is copied to
`%LOCALAPPDATA%\Programs\gorbe` and added to the user `PATH`.

## Usage

Run `gorbe` with no arguments for the interactive prompt, or use any of these
options:

| Option | Description |
| ------ | ----------- |
| `--name NAME` | Project name. |
| `--framework {fastapi,django,flask}` | Framework to use. |
| `--database {sqlite,mysql,postgresql}` | Database to configure. |
| `--manager {pip,uv}` | Package manager to use. |
| `--docker`, `--no-docker` | Generate Docker files. |
| `--path PATH` | Directory in which to create the project. |
| `--db-name NAME` | Database name used in Docker files. |
| `--db-user USER` | Database user used in Docker files. |
| `--db-password PASSWORD` | Database password used in Docker files. |
| `--db-root-password PASSWORD` | MySQL root password used in Docker files. |
| `--version` | Print the version and exit. |

When an option is omitted, Gorbe asks for it interactively. Database credentials
are only prompted for when Docker files are requested with MySQL or PostgreSQL.

## Generated project

FastAPI and Flask projects use the same layout:

```
my-app/
├── app/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── main.py
│   ├── router.py          # FastAPI
│   ├── schema.py          # FastAPI
│   ├── database.py
│   └── models.py
├── .git/
├── .gitignore
├── .venv/
├── requirements.txt
├── pyproject.toml         # uv only
├── uv.lock                # uv only
├── Dockerfile             # optional
├── .dockerignore          # optional
└── docker-compose.yaml    # optional
```

Django projects are created at the project root:

```
my-app/
├── manage.py
├── my_app_django/
│   └── settings.py
├── .git/
├── .gitignore
├── .venv/
├── requirements.txt
└── ...
```

Dependencies are installed automatically. For pip projects, activate the
virtual environment before running:

```bash
source my-app/.venv/bin/activate
uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

For uv projects:

```bash
cd my-app
uv run uvicorn app.main:app --reload
```

## Databases

FastAPI uses async SQLAlchemy; Flask uses sync SQLAlchemy.

| Database | FastAPI driver | Flask driver |
| -------- | -------------- | ------------ |
| SQLite | `aiosqlite` | built in |
| MySQL | `aiomysql` | `pymysql` |
| PostgreSQL | `asyncpg` | `psycopg` |

The generated database module reads `DATABASE_URL` from the environment and
falls back to a local default. Docker Compose sets this variable automatically
for the selected database.

Django projects keep Django's default SQLite configuration. The database option
only affects the generated Docker database service for Django projects.

## Docker

Generate a project with Docker files and start it with:

```bash
cd my-app
docker compose up --build
```

FastAPI and Django are exposed on port `8000`; Flask is exposed on port `5000`.
MySQL and PostgreSQL services include a persistent volume and a healthcheck.

## Development

```bash
uv sync --extra dev
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check .
```

